. This information helps us to improve site navigation and to make improvements to the site and content.\n\nPlease be aware that if you voluntarily disclose information over the Internet, personal or otherwise, the information is subject to review and collection by unintended third parties. For example, if you email us, it might be possible for other unintended readers to read the contents of your email. We have no means to control this.\n<br></div><div>\n<span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\">How We Use Collected Information</span></span></div><div>\nWe record IP addresses for systems administration purposes to obtain data for technical analysis to improve the performance of the website.All communications from you to the website are indexed for technical reasons. For example, it you summit a helpful comment, we keep a record of the information for use by our developers and managers to improve the site. A copy of most messages sent by email is forwarded to our confidential archives, where developers and managers can use the information to make system improvements on a confidential basis and solely for internal purposes and to monitor traffic flow and user satisfaction.When we collect personal information on the order forms, the information is used solely to facilitate the purchase transaction. We follow strict procedures to exchange the necessary payment information with the appropriate financial organizations.\n<br></div><div>\n<span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\">Our Cookies</span></span></div><div>\nYour browser offers so-called “cookies” which — if you allow their use — store small amounts of data on your computer about your visit to our website. Cookies assist us in tracking which of the website features you like best. However, cookies do not disclose any personal information.\n<br></div><div>\n<span style=\"font-size: 18px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 28px;\">Third Party Cookies</span></span></div><div>\nT